From 1cfadb730e792a3677a547a8a70ab993c4b010aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: floating windows move together with the rest, and every
 question to the window system is counted

A camera move told the window system beforehand which docked windows it was about to move, so that their apps could work side by
side. Floating windows still went one at a time, each waiting for its app's answer.

- `placeFloatingWindows` makes its plan, foretells from that very plan (`movesInSight(in:on:reason:)`), and walks it. Not together with
  the docked windows: floating windows are placed last, after the rounds in which a window that refuses its slot has the layout
  reckoned again, and the Desktop may be elsewhere by then. Foretold from the first layout, a floating window went where the
  final plan never sent it: twice on its way at best. `aLayoutReckonedAgainSendsNoFloatingWindowAnywhereTwice` holds that down.
- With `shrinkOutOfView` nothing is foretold at the size a window has, because it is parked at another.
- `Budget.questions` and `Budget.windowLists`: the fake counts every question it is asked. A command has the window server list
  every window once at most (an app's quit twice, a start three times); seven everyday commands not at all.
- `arbor-sim bench` prints what each command asks. A big desk for a benchmark is built once and kept.
